  "body": {
    "id": "lem:martingale-centering",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "The block scores satisfy \\(\\mathbb E(R_b\\mid\\mathcal F_{b-1})=0\\), and \\(\\sqrt{GB}(\\widehat\\tau-\\tau)=B^{-1/2}\\sum_{b\\in\\mathcal B_B}R_b\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "R_b",
      "\\mathcal F_b",
      "G",
      "B",
      "\\widehat\\tau",
      "\\tau",
      "\\mathcal B_B"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:nonanticipation",
      "ass:finite-memory-lag-one",
      "prop:exact-unbiasedness",
      "lem:score-decomposition"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "By \\(\\texttt{prop:exact-unbiasedness}\\), conditional on \\(\\mathcal F_{b-1}\\), \\(\\mathbb E(\\widehat\\tau_b\\mid\\mathcal F_{b-1})=\\tau_b\\).  Assumptions \\(\\texttt{ass:nonanticipation}\\) and \\(\\texttt{ass:finite-memory-lag-one}\\) ensure that \\(\\tau_b\\), which uses the two-period sustained-exposure endpoints of block \\(b\\), is a fixed finite-population contrast rather than a function of the current random draw.  Therefore\n\\[\n \\mathbb E(R_b\\mid\\mathcal F_{b-1})\n =\\sqrt G\\{\\mathbb E(\\widehat\\tau_b\\mid\\mathcal F_{b-1})-\\tau_b\\}=0.\n\\]\nMoreover, the definitions of \\(\\widehat\\tau\\), \\(\\tau\\), and \\(R_b\\) give the pathwise identity\n\\[\n \\sqrt{GB}(\\widehat\\tau-\\tau)\n =\\frac{\\sqrt{GB}}B\\sum_{b=1}^B(\\widehat\\tau_b-\\tau_b)\n =B^{-1/2}\\sum_{b=1}^BR_b.\n\\]",
    "justification": "Predictable centering makes the across-block accumulation a design-based martingale rather than a pseudo-target drift.",
    "gap": "LiZhao2026Adaptive supplies the general adaptive martingale template, including sequential rerandomization, but leaves to the present design the conditional derivation that the fixed-half first stage plus fixed-count second stage produces a centered joint score for the sustained lag-one endpoint target.",
    "consumer": "This identity supplies the filtration structure needed for the root-\\(GB\\) limit law.",
